    "answer": {
      "short": "$200$. There are $250\\div5=50$ multiples of $5$, leaving $250-50=200$ numbers.",
      "worked": "Every fifth number from $1$ to $250$ is a multiple of $5$, so there are $250\\div5=50$ multiples of $5$. There are $250$ whole numbers in the range. Therefore, $250-50=200$ are not divisible by $5$.",
